{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Agreement is recited as \"made by and between\" EGL and the Borrower, yet only EGL grants the guarantee, so whether Essar Steel Minnesota is a bound party is unclear against Section 2.02(d) and (f), which impose affirmative obligations on the Borrower. The preamble also names the Facility Agent as the party in whose favor it is made while the recitals speak of the ratable benefit of the Lenders.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.2}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The recital states the guarantee is delivered \"for the ratable benefit of the Lenders,\" which sits against the operative preamble and Section 4.15, under which the Agreement runs in favor of the Facility Agent and confers rights only on Lenders. A party could argue the recital controls who may enforce.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Wholesale incorporation of the Credit Agreement's defined terms cannot be squared with Section 4.14 (Entire Agreement), which declares this Agreement alone the entire agreement and supersedes all prior agreements on the subject matter. Which document supplies meaning is then contestable.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.2}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Agreement\" is defined as subject to being \"restated, amended, supplemented or otherwise modified from time to time,\" but the instrument contains no amendment provision and Section 4.01 points only to Section 4.12 (Notices) for written instruments. How an amendment is validly made is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The catch-all \"all other obligations and liabilities of the Borrower ... which may arise under, out of, or in connection with\" the Loan Documents follows an enumeration of principal, interest and LC Exposure, leaving the guaranteed universe without a boundary. Section 1.02(e) expressly disclaims ejusdem generis, sharpening the fight over scope.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.2}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
   {"issue": "A \"Deficiency\" is what is \"determined by the Borrower or the Required Lenders,\" giving two independent determiners with no rule for conflicting or competing determinations and no standard of determination. Whether either determination binds the Guarantor is unresolved.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
   {"issue": "Clause (ii) does not read grammatically onto the lead-in (\"shortfall ... required: ... any increase in the cost of the Project\") and largely duplicates clause (i), which already covers costs above US$1,097,000,000 outside a Permitted Project Change. The two limbs cannot be given distinct content as drafted.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.25}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The release condition turns on offtake agreements \"in form and substance and for a term ... reasonably acceptable\" to 66 2/3% Lenders and on an offtaker \"reasonably acceptable\" to them, with no objective benchmark or outside date. Whether the guarantee is ever released is thus committed to a reasonableness standard a court would have to construe.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.45}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The proviso obliges Lenders only to \"negotiate in good faith\" over a \"draft pellet purchase agreement that would be reasonably acceptable,\" an agreement to agree with no standard of compliance or consequence for failure. It is also a Lender obligation buried inside a definition.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.35}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Material adverse effect on the business, financial condition, operations or performance or properties of the Guarantor since the date of this Agreement\" supplies no benchmark or magnitude for materiality and the trailing \"since the date of this Agreement\" has no clear grammatical anchor. The term drives paragraphs (a), (c), (d) and (m) of Article III.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Obligations\" is defined as the Borrower Obligations, while \"Borrower Obligations\" is itself defined by reference to \"the Obligations (as defined in the Credit Agreement),\" creating a circular definitional loop between this provision and the Borrower Obligations definition. Which \"Obligations\" is meant in Sections 4.02(c) and elsewhere is then uncertain.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause is truncated — \"words importing any gender include the other\" omits the noun it governs — so the rule has no stated object. A mechanical omission of this kind leaves the interpretive rule incomplete on its face.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.1}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This rule abolishes ejusdem generis and expressio unius for every list in the instrument, which cannot be comfortably squared with enumerations elsewhere that appear closed — the two-limb \"Deficiency\" definition and the two permitted funding forms in Section 2.02(d). Whether those lists are exhaustive is thrown into doubt.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.2}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c020", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Permitted successors and assigns ... not prohibited by the terms hereof\" depends on the assignment rules, but Sections 4.03 and 4.15 state different consent requirements for the same act. What counts as a permitted assign is therefore indeterminate.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.1}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c021", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c022", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Section 1.03 makes this Agreement govern over any conflicting Loan Document, yet Section 1.01, Section 2.02(d), the last sentence of Section 2.03 (Credit Agreement Section 6.07) and Section 4.12 all subordinate this Agreement's operation to the Credit Agreement. Which instrument controls in a conflict is left genuinely open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.3}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c023", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The three guarantee periods do not fit together: clause (i) runs only until the Credit Agreement conditions in \"Sections 4.01 through 4.02\" are satisfied (skipping Section 4.03), clause (iii) begins only at the Commercial Operations Date, leaving an interval covered by nothing but the Deficiency undertaking, and the $250,000,000 cap is expressed to apply only \"under this clause (iii).\" Whether EGL's exposure is capped at all, and when, is the central construction question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.47},
   {"issue": "The temporal limits on clauses (i) and (ii) cannot be squared with Section 2.01(d), which says the guarantee \"contained in this Section 2.01\" remains in full force until the earlier of the EGL Guarantee Release Date or payment in full. One provision ends the guarantee on satisfaction of conditions precedent; the other keeps it alive.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.3}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c024", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The sentence is broken — \"the obligations of the Guarantor hereunder are primary and notwithstanding the obligations of any other Person providing any Guarantee, Collateral or other assurance\" leaves the \"notwithstanding\" limb without a predicate. What effect the other credit support has on EGL's primary liability cannot be read off the words.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c025", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The savings cap is measured by \"applicable federal and state laws relating to fraudulent conveyances,\" although the Guarantor is a Cayman Islands company and the instrument is New York-governed, so which body of law fixes the ceiling is unstated. It also purports to cap liability \"under the other Loan Documents,\" reaching beyond this Agreement.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c026", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c027", "issues": [
